  <prompt>
    Execute Track-B batch 3 of FR-TB-01: delete the five dead PCF directories and the R1-era client-shared deadwood (registries, providers, cross-pane mechanisms) from inventory §9. The PCF dirs are empty or source-less orphaned build artifacts; the client-shared items are superseded — AI.Outputs' R1 registries lost to the canonical R2 registries in `Spaarke.AI.Widgets`, and the CustomEvent/BroadcastChannel cross-pane mechanisms lost to `PaneEventBus`. This batch rides alongside wave W-P0-C. Per NFR-08, every deletion is grep-zero-verified with SHOWN output and builds proven green; evidence lands in `notes/track-b/batch-3-evidence.md`.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Frontend developer familiar with the Spaarke client estate — PCF control layout under `src/client/pcf/`, the shared packages (`Spaarke.UI.Components`, AI.Context, AI.Outputs, `Spaarke.AI.Widgets`) — and careful about package export barrels when deleting modules.
  </role>

  <goal>
    Every batch-3 item below is deleted (or recorded keep-with-reason if found live), grep-zero shown per deleted symbol, `npm run build:prod` green for every touched client package with shown output, TASK-INDEX updated, and `notes/track-b/batch-3-evidence.md` written.
  </goal>

  <inputs>
    <file purpose="design-spec">projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r1/spec.md</file>
    <file purpose="project-plan">projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r1/plan.md</file>
    <file purpose="project-context">projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r1/CLAUDE.md</file>
    <file purpose="task-index">projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r1/tasks/TASK-INDEX.md</file>
    <file purpose="deadwood-register">projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r1/notes/audit-inputs/SPAARKE-AI-CODE-INVENTORY.md</file>
    <file purpose="delete-list">projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r1/notes/audit-inputs/SPAARKE-AI-MIGRATION-MAP.md</file>
  </inputs>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Do not modify files outside the batch list; deadwood only — if a batch item turns out to be live, STOP and record keep-with-reason instead of deleting.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-08">Every retirement verified grep-zero with SHOWN output; no compat shims retained.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The canonical R2 registries (`WorkspaceWidgetRegistry` / `ContextWidgetRegistry` in Spaarke.AI.Widgets) and `PaneEventBus` are LIVE — only the AI.Outputs R1 `output-registry`/`source-registry` and the superseded cross-pane mechanisms delete. Verify names precisely before deleting.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">When deleting exported modules, update the package barrel (index.ts) exports in the same change so builds stay green.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Deleted tests of dead components are SCAFFOLDING class — record in the evidence file for task-090 /test-diet reconciliation.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>pcf, client-shared/dead-code-removal, track-b</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r1/plan.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r1/notes/audit-inputs/SPAARKE-AI-MIGRATION-MAP.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r1/notes/audit-inputs/SPAARKE-AI-CODE-INVENTORY.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r1/notes/audit-inputs/OVERLAY-MATRIX.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/SPAARKEAI-COMPONENT-MODEL.md</file>
      <file>src/client/pcf/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <context>
    <background>
      Batch contents (inventory §9 "Client shared" + "PCF" + migration-map start-now list):
      (1) five dead PCF dirs — `AIMetadataExtractor` (empty), `AnalysisWorkspace`, `AnalysisBuilder`, `PlaybookBuilderHost`, `DrillThroughWorkspace` (source-less orphaned build artifacts) under `src/client/pcf/`;
      (2) `StandaloneAiProvider` + `useStandaloneAi` (AI.Context);
      (3) AI.Outputs R1 `output-registry` + `source-registry` (dead — canonical registries live in Spaarke.AI.Widgets);
      (4) the 4 unregistered AI.Outputs widgets: Chart, DataTable, Timeline, DocumentCompare;
      (5) AI.Outputs `cross-pane/` (CustomEvent mechanism, superseded by PaneEventBus);
      (6) `SprkChatExportWord`;
      (7) `SprkChatBridge` (BroadcastChannel, @deprecated, superseded by PaneEventBus).
    </background>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="none" status="complete">No dependencies — rides wave W-P0-C.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
    <related-work>
      <item>Task 050 (FR-P4-01) completion audit consumes this batch's evidence file</item>
      <item>Task 046 (FR-P3-07) dedupes the two register-context-widgets modules — separate scope; do not touch here</item>
    </related-work>
  </context>

  <steps>
    <step order="0" name="Context check">
      Check context usage. If &gt; 70%, create handoff summary and request new chat. Load inputs; read inventory §9 (Client shared + PCF) and §6 (registry liveness verdicts).
    </step>
    <step order="1" name="Read and confirm the batch list">
      Locate every item via Glob/Grep with exact paths; confirm the five PCF dirs are source-less/empty and each client-shared item has zero live importers. Distinguish the dead AI.Outputs R1 registries from the live Spaarke.AI.Widgets registries by path. Any live item → keep-with-reason.
    </step>
    <step order="2" name="Delete the batch">
      Delete the five PCF directories and the confirmed-dead client-shared modules + their tests; update package barrels/exports so nothing dangles.
    </step>
    <step order="3" name="Grep-zero verification (SHOWN)">
      For each deleted symbol (`AIMetadataExtractor`, `AnalysisWorkspace` (PCF), `AnalysisBuilder`, `PlaybookBuilderHost`, `DrillThroughWorkspace`, `StandaloneAiProvider`, `useStandaloneAi`, `output-registry`, `source-registry`, the four widget names, `cross-pane`, `SprkChatExportWord`, `SprkChatBridge`): grep across src/ and SHOW zero-hit output; note intentional same-name survivors (e.g., live code-page `AnalysisWorkspace` directories vs the dead PCF dir) explicitly with paths.
    </step>
    <step order="4" name="Build verification (SHOWN)">
      Run `npm run build:prod` for every touched package/solution (AI.Context, AI.Outputs, shared UI lib as applicable); show green output. Run touched-surface tests.
    </step>
    <step order="5" name="Evidence + close">
      Write `projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r1/notes/track-b/batch-3-evidence.md` (item table: deleted-path / grep output / keep-with-reason). Update TASK-INDEX.md (072 → ✅). Report completion.
    </step>
  </steps>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">build:prod + tests for touched client packages</tool>
    <tool name="git">Version control (deletions preserved in history)</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/pcf/ (5 dead control dirs removed)</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/ (AI.Context + AI.Outputs deadwood removed, barrels updated)</output>
    <output type="report">projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r1/notes/track-b/batch-3-evidence.md</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r1/tasks/TASK-INDEX.md (status update)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Per-batch grep-zero for every deleted symbol outside git history, with output SHOWN (FR-TB-01 / NFR-08).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">npm run build:prod green for every touched client package with output shown.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Live registries (Spaarke.AI.Widgets) and PaneEventBus untouched; any live-found batch item recorded keep-with-reason.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">notes/track-b/batch-3-evidence.md exists with the per-item evidence table; TASK-INDEX updated.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <execution>
